
To optimize the creation of 500+ records, the issue is almost certainly Database Round-Trips.
Currently, your application is likely doing this:
 * Ask DB for an ID (Round trip 1)
 * Insert Row 1 (Round trip 2)
 * Ask DB for next ID (Round trip 3)
 * Insert Row 2 (Round trip 4)
   ...
   For 500 records, that is 1000 network calls to the database. This is why it hangs.
We need to enable JDBC Batching and Sequence Allocation Optimization. This will reduce those 1000 calls down to about 5 or 10 calls.
Here is the optimized code and the required steps.
🚀 Step 1: Update application.properties (Crucial)
Add these lines to your src/main/resources/application.properties. This forces Hibernate to group SQL statements together.
# Optimization for Bulk Inserts
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.jdbc.batch_size=50
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.order_inserts=true
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.order_updates=true
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.jdbc.batch_versioned_data=true

🚀 Step 2: Update Entities (Change Allocation Size)
We need to change allocationSize = 1 to allocationSize = 50. This allows Java to fetch 50 IDs in one go, instead of asking the DB every single time.
